    "body": "## Why\n\nMerging #167 advanced main to `b21cce4c8661589267ad5719f850accbec088d2f` and left #169 conflicted. This successor applies the reviewed snapshot writer changes on that main while preserving the complete validation implementation now on main.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Apply the seven exact product files already reviewed for #169. The complete resulting `crates/`, `Cargo.toml`, and `Cargo.lock` match its fixed G2 product.\n- Batch the six snapshot leaf tables within one file and table, retaining bounded 64/8/1 row groups and the existing single-row path for oversized values. Preserve transaction, identity, FTS, ordering, and error behavior.\n- Include the reviewed snapshot regression tests and their explicit `Vec<String>` compiler fix. The seventh file contains the previously reviewed equivalent `Option::is_none_or` spelling only.\n- Retain all 138 ordinary validation inputs from current main. The v15 verifier changes only its four product/review/path/digest constants, with a matching full registry; proof functions, original CI, and six frozen v14 inputs are unchanged.\n\n## Review and validation\n\nIndependent review binds all 1089 product inputs, the 41 deltas from the historical base, and all 138 validation inputs. Separate actual Git-object review confirms the P3 → R3 → G3 chain and unchanged file modes.\n\n- Product: `90838d6c890b12f031fa0be9d1956cfbdef9e8d6`\n- Independent review commit: `b0f0c0d00e38508e7e43b0e87d1215d7f6413969`\n- Fixed candidate: `26768b5e38ed1784bf77a8c4fe57baf01a19c626`\n- [Canonical independent review](https://github.com/jyqj/codecortex/blob/26768b5e38ed1784bf77a8c4fe57baf01a19c626/artifacts/checkpoints/p8-mainb21-snapshot-leaf-integration-20261009/independent-source-review.json)\n\nThis draft awaits its own original CI and source-integrity proof. G2's prior CI, 53 targeted Rust tests, and 50 Python methods remain evidence for their original fixed source and runs. The ongoing original 100k engineering observation and a23 formal 150-shard study retain their original commits and plans.\n\n## Task status\n\nNo TODO is closed by this integration or by opening this PR: 163 done, 29 remaining. The a23 ten-task closeout remains governed by its own original acceptance evidence; this optional integration adds no prerequisite to it. #169 and its original failures and measurement history remain preserved.\n",
